{"dir":"c2s","kind":"notification","method":"textDocument/didOpen","params":{"textDocument":{"languageId":"wolf","text":"//! check: run(exit=0, stdout=\"wolf é | 7 | true | 836 | 195 169 | true\")\n//! phase: run\n//! conforms: type.byte, type.byte.cast, type.byte.op, str.views\n//!\n//! s136 (#231) — `bytes()` speaks bytes. The view's element is a\n//! `byte` ([type.byte], D72): `let bs = s.bytes()` is a `List[byte]`,\n//! `str_from_utf8(bs)` takes it back without a conversion (the\n//! round trip is the witness that producer and consumer agree on the\n//! type), a byte pushed into a `List[byte]` is the octet itself, the\n//! walk's sum widens at `+` ([type.byte.op]) and an element read\n//! against an `int` is spelled `as int` ([type.byte.cast]) — the\n//! one spelling every program that did arithmetic on a `.bytes()`\n//! element without it now reads in the E0401 note\n//! (`typecheck/byte_elem_arith_fail.lu`).\n\nfn dup(bs: List[byte]) -> List[byte] {\n    var out = List[byte]()\n    for b in bs {\n        (mut out).push(b)\n    }\n    out\n}\n\nfn main() -> !int {\n    let s = \"wolf é\"\n    let bs = s.bytes()\n    let back = str_from_utf8(bs)?\n    let same = back == s\n    var sum = 0\n    for b in s.bytes() {\n        sum = sum + b\n    }\n    let lead = bs[5] as int\n    let cont = bs[6] as int\n    let dup = dup(bs)\n    let twice = str_from_utf8(dup)?\n    let again = twice == s && dup.len == bs.len\n    print(\"{back} | {bs.len} | {same} | {sum} | {lead} {cont} | {again}\")\n    if !same { return 1 }\n    if !again { return 2 }\n    0\n}\n","uri":"file://$WS/strings/bytes_roundtrip.lu","version":1}},"seq":4}
